<item><title>What remains of canned Portal prequel white whale F-Stop is now fully playable thanks to modders and some big leaks</title><link>https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/what-remains-of-canned-portal-prequel-white-whale-f-stop-is-now-fully-playable-thanks-to-modders-and-some-big-leaks</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Oisin Kuhnke</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 19:08:44 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/what-remains-of-canned-portal-prequel-white-whale-f-stop-is-now-fully-playable-thanks-to-modders-and-some-big-leaks</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Android</category><category>EA Partners</category><category>Electronic Arts</category><category>First person</category><category>Mac</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>PC</category><category>Platformer</category><category>Portal</category><category>Portal 2</category><category>PS3</category><category>Puzzle</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Valve</category><category>Valve Corporation</category><category>Valve Software</category><category>Xbox 360</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/fstop_3YhkRv1.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/fstop_3YhkRv1.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>
If you're something of a Portal or <a href="https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/games/half-life">Half-Life</a> head, you'll probably already be familiar with F-Stop, an unreleased Portal prequel that remained quite mysterious for many years. <a href="https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/f-stop-the-secret-mechanic-of-valves-unreleased-portal-prequel-has-finally-been-revealed">Back in 2020</a>, a much deeper look was revealed in a semi-official capacity, revealing a pretty neat concept (that isn't so dissimilar to that of Superliminal). Now, all these years later, assets and source code for the game has leaked, and what exists of F-Stop is fully playable.
</p> <p><a href="https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/what-remains-of-canned-portal-prequel-white-whale-f-stop-is-now-fully-playable-thanks-to-modders-and-some-big-leaks">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item>
<item><title>Final Fantasy 14: Evercold sets itself a release date at the tail end of winter, alongside offering a look at its second, avian-inclined new job</title><link>https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/final-fantasy-14-evercold-sets-itself-a-release-date-at-the-tail-end-of-winter-alongside-offering-a-look-at-its-second-avian-inclined-new-job</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Oisin Kuhnke</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 18:07:48 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/final-fantasy-14-evercold-sets-itself-a-release-date-at-the-tail-end-of-winter-alongside-offering-a-look-at-its-second-avian-inclined-new-job</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Fantasy</category><category>Final Fantasy XIV: A Realm Reborn - Collector's Edition</category><category>Final Fantasy XIV: Evercold</category><category>JRPG</category><category>Mac</category><category>MMO</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Open World</category><category>PC</category><category>PS3</category><category>PS4</category><category>PS5</category><category>RPG</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Square Enix</category><category>Third person</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/final-fantasy-14-evercold-zephyr.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/final-fantasy-14-evercold-zephyr.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>
Let's start with the bad news: <a href="https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/games/final-fantasy-xiv-evervold">Final Fantasy 14: Evercold</a> has been delayed. The good news, that doesn't matter all that much, as it's only a delay of roughly a month, and a release date has been set in stone too: February 23rd, 2027. It's cutting it a bit close to the seasons shifting towards spring, making the game seasonally inappropriate, but hey ho, February is still winter!
